{
  "description": "Add getPolicyFileDetails for GET /tailnet/{tailnet}/acl?details=true. The spec documents details only as a query parameter on getPolicyFile, whose response the hujson patch types as raw HuJSON text, but with details=true the body is JSON {acl: base64 of the HuJSON, warnings: string[], errors: string[]} (the spec's details description and its exampleWithDetails, which sends errors: null; tailscale/tailscale client/tailscale/acl.go (3ec5be3f5) ACLHuJSON decodes acl and warnings from it and reads the ETag header). getPolicyFile loses details, and the new operation returns the JSON typed, warnings and errors nullable.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileRequest/members/details"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsRequest",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {},
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#input": {}
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "copy",
      "from": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileRequest/members/tailnet",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsRequest/members/tailnet"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsResponseWarningsList",
      "value": {
        "type": "list",
        "member": {
          "target": "smithy.api#String"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsResponseErrorsList",
      "value": {
        "type": "list",
        "member": {
          "target": "smithy.api#String"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsResponse",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
          "acl": {
            "target": "smithy.api#String",
            "traits": {
              "smithy.api#required": {},
              "smithy.api#documentation": "The policy file's HuJSON text, base64-encoded."
            }
          },
          "warnings": {
            "target": "com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsResponseWarningsList",
            "traits": {
              "smithy.api#required": {},
              "com.distilled.openapi#nullable": {},
              "smithy.api#documentation": "Syntactically valid but nonsensical entries."
            }
          },
          "errors": {
            "target": "com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsResponseErrorsList",
            "traits": {
              "smithy.api#required": {},
              "com.distilled.openapi#nullable": {},
              "smithy.api#documentation": "Parsing failures."
            }
          },
          "eTag": {
            "target": "smithy.api#String",
            "traits": {
              "smithy.api#httpHeader": "ETag",
              "smithy.api#documentation": "Entity tag for the policy file. Send it back as If-Match on setPolicyFile."
            }
          }
        },
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#output": {}
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetails",
      "value": {
        "type": "operation",
        "input": {
          "target": "com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsRequest"
        },
        "output": {
          "target": "com.tailscale.api#GetPolicyFileDetailsResponse"
        },
        "errors": [
          {
            "target": "com.tailscale.api#BadRequest"
          },
          {
            "target": "com.tailscale.api#Forbidden"
          },
          {
            "target": "com.tailscale.api#NotFound"
          },
          {
            "target": "com.tailscale.api#TailnetNotFound"
          }
        ],
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "uri": "/tailnet/{tailnet}/acl?details=true",
            "code": 200
          },
          "smithy.api#documentation": "Get policy file details\n\nRetrieves the current policy file for the given tailnet with `details=true`: the HuJSON text base64-encoded as `acl`, with the `warnings` and `errors` Tailscale found in it. The response also includes the `ETag` header.\n\nOAuth Scope: `policy_file:read`."
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
